   "x": "Nuclear Thermal Propulsion, in which a reactor heats liquid hydrogen, gives high thrust, not low continuous thrust. Low continuous thrust is a feature of Nuclear Electric Propulsion. An RTG uses plutonium-238 decay heat for a few hundred watts, and a compact fission reactor gives 10-100 kW."
